  "text": "Find the expression for the length \n𝑎\n(\n𝑥\n)\n in terms of \n𝑥\n.\n𝑎\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n \n2√x+1\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nLet's consider the right triangle formed by two sides and a diagonal.\n\nAccording to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n(\n𝑥\n+\n2\n)\n2\n\t\n=\n𝑥\n2\n+\n𝑎\n2\n\n\n𝑎\n2\n\t\n=\n(\n𝑥\n+\n2\n)\n2\n−\n𝑥\n2\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n(\n𝑥\n+\n2\n)\n2\n−\n𝑥\n2\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n𝑥\n2\n+\n4\n𝑥\n+\n4\n−\n𝑥\n2\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n4\n𝑥\n+\n4\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n4\n(\n𝑥\n+\n1\n)\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n4\n⋅\n𝑥\n+\n1\n\n\n𝑎\n\t\n=\n2\n𝑥\n+\n1\n."
}